WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.931
It was a lovely summer day in the country.

2
00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:12.333
Mother Duck sat on her eggs for a long time.

3
00:00:13.153 --> 00:00:17.315
After a while, one by one, ducklings came out of the eggs.

4
00:00:17.335 --> 00:00:20.496
"Peep, peep!

5
00:00:21.097 --> 00:00:23.257
Peep, peep!"

6
00:00:23.277 --> 00:00:24.238
"Quack, quack!

7
00:00:24.618 --> 00:00:25.518
Are you all out?"

8
00:00:26.979 --> 00:00:29.020
"No, one egg is still here.

9
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.240
Look how big it is!"

10
00:00:33.941 --> 00:00:35.882
At last the big egg hatched.

11
00:00:36.442 --> 00:00:39.523
This duckling was very big and very ugly.

12
00:00:39.543 --> 00:00:41.903
"Oh my!

13
00:00:42.444 --> 00:00:46.004
This duckling is big and different from the others.

14
00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:48.385
I wonder if it is a turkey.

15
00:00:48.745 --> 00:00:50.346
We will soon find out."

16
00:00:51.986 --> 00:00:54.047
Mother Duck took her ducklings to the water.

17
00:00:54.947 --> 00:00:58.668
One after another the little ducklings jumped into the water.

18
00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:03.415
The ugly duckling also jumped into the water and swam very well.

19
00:01:03.435 --> 00:01:08.099
"Oh, he is not a turkey.

20
00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:09.761
Turkeys can't swim.

21
00:01:10.241 --> 00:01:11.382
He is a duckling.

22
00:01:11.863 --> 00:01:13.464
Let's go to the farmyard.

23
00:01:13.865 --> 00:01:17.488
But you must stay close to me and watch out for the cat."

24
00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:21.071
"Look at that duckling!

25
00:01:21.131 --> 00:01:23.393
He looks so strange."

26
00:01:23.933 --> 00:01:25.655
"He is so big and ugly.

27
00:01:25.955 --> 00:01:26.696
Go away!"

28
00:01:27.404 --> 00:01:29.526
"Please, leave him alone.

29
00:01:29.546 --> 00:01:31.928
He is not doing any harm."

30
00:01:33.209 --> 00:01:35.831
But the ducks pecked the ugly duckling.

31
00:01:36.232 --> 00:01:40.015
All the animals in the farmyard bit him and pushed him too.

32
00:01:40.035 --> 00:01:44.378
"I wish the cat would eat you!"

33
00:01:44.398 --> 00:01:47.941
"You should never have been born."

34
00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.386
So the poor little duckling was very sad.

35
00:01:54.207 --> 00:01:55.668
Finally he ran away.

36
00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.142
"Why does everyone hate me?

37
00:02:00.642 --> 00:02:02.584
Is it because I am so ugly?

38
00:02:03.204 --> 00:02:04.945
But I am really nice."

39
00:02:06.627 --> 00:02:08.849
The ugly duckling met two wild ducks.

40
00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:12.011
"What kind of duck are you?"

41
00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.672
"You are really ugly.

42
00:02:13.993 --> 00:02:17.155
But that's okay if you don't marry a duck from our family."

43
00:02:18.997 --> 00:02:21.999
Then the ugly duckling heard pop, pop!

44
00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:24.781
And the two wild ducks fell dead.

45
00:02:27.043 --> 00:02:29.909
Just then many hunting dogs appeared.

46
00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:32.431
The ugly duckling was very afraid.

47
00:02:33.171 --> 00:02:35.133
So he tucked his head under his wing.

48
00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:38.035
A hunting dog sniffed the ugly duckling.

49
00:02:39.015 --> 00:02:39.816
"Sniff, sniff!

50
00:02:40.736 --> 00:02:41.677
You are ugly!"

51
00:02:42.578 --> 00:02:45.139
And they went away without touching the ugly duckling.

52
00:02:45.159 --> 00:02:49.002
"Oh, I am alive!

53
00:02:49.682 --> 00:02:50.903
No one wants me.

54
00:02:51.484 --> 00:02:53.985
Even a dog doesn't want to bite me."

55
00:02:54.986 --> 00:02:58.648
He felt lucky, but at the same time he felt sad.

56
00:02:59.489 --> 00:03:02.710
The poor duckling waited for several hours and then ran away.

57
00:03:06.071 --> 00:03:06.952
A storm began.

58
00:03:07.512 --> 00:03:10.133
The rain and lightning terrified the ugly duckling.

59
00:03:10.873 --> 00:03:12.334
He was so cold and wet!

60
00:03:12.774 --> 00:03:15.876
He ran and ran as he looked for shelter from the storm.

61
00:03:18.857 --> 00:03:20.738
Finally he arrived at a cottage.

62
00:03:21.478 --> 00:03:24.819
An old woman, a cat, and a hen lived in this cottage.

63
00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.280
He went inside.

64
00:03:27.884 --> 00:03:29.425
"May I have some food?"

65
00:03:30.146 --> 00:03:31.547
"Oh, what a prize!

66
00:03:32.308 --> 00:03:33.509
Is it a fat duck?

67
00:03:34.229 --> 00:03:36.231
Now I can have duck eggs."

68
00:03:37.732 --> 00:03:39.574
The old woman's sight was very bad.

69
00:03:40.455 --> 00:03:42.596
So the duckling lived there for a few days.

70
00:03:44.158 --> 00:03:46.900
But the hen and the cat were mean to the duckling.

71
00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:48.501
"I can lay eggs.

72
00:03:48.822 --> 00:03:49.662
Can you do that?"

73
00:03:49.682 --> 00:03:53.606
"No." "I can catch a mouse.

74
00:03:54.006 --> 00:03:54.867
Can you do that?"

75
00:03:54.887 --> 00:03:58.961
"No." "Then what can you do?"

76
00:03:58.981 --> 00:04:00.662
"I can swim."

77
00:04:00.682 --> 00:04:03.843
"Oh, no one should swim!

78
00:04:04.403 --> 00:04:05.884
You will surely drown!"

79
00:04:05.904 --> 00:04:07.625
"I won't drown."

80
00:04:07.645 --> 00:04:10.346
"You are a big liar!"

81
00:04:10.946 --> 00:04:12.907
So the poor duckling left the cottage.

82
00:04:15.368 --> 00:04:17.369
Soon summer turned into fall.

83
00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:20.150
The ugly duckling swam in the pond.

84
00:04:20.911 --> 00:04:22.912
A group of swans flew over the duckling.

85
00:04:25.244 --> 00:04:27.125
"What beautiful birds!

86
00:04:27.906 --> 00:04:29.546
I wish I could be like them."

87
00:04:31.027 --> 00:04:32.688
The weather grew colder and colder.

88
00:04:33.309 --> 00:04:34.249
Then winter came.

89
00:04:34.269 --> 00:04:40.793
"I must swim and swim, or the pond will freeze around me."

90
00:04:42.313 --> 00:04:45.075
But every night the ice grew thicker and thicker.

91
00:04:45.955 --> 00:04:50.198
Finally the pond froze over, and the duckling couldn't move anymore.

92
00:04:53.179 --> 00:04:56.345
Early in the morning, a farmer saw the frozen duckling.

93
00:04:57.605 --> 00:04:59.586
"Oh, poor duckling!

94
00:05:00.006 --> 00:05:02.787
I'll take you home to my wife and children."

95
00:05:04.248 --> 00:05:05.929
The wife took care of the duckling.

96
00:05:06.649 --> 00:05:08.110
Soon the duckling got well.

97
00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:12.331
But the children wanted to play with the duckling.

98
00:05:12.611 --> 00:05:15.072
"Come and play with us!

99
00:05:15.372 --> 00:05:16.773
Come and play with us!"

100
00:05:18.674 --> 00:05:19.774
The duckling was scared.

101
00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:25.476
The farmer's wife and the children chased the duckling around the farm house.

102
00:05:25.496 --> 00:05:27.078
Finally he ran out the door.

103
00:05:32.582 --> 00:05:34.664
Spring came and everything was beautiful.

104
00:05:35.424 --> 00:05:39.608
The ugly duckling saw the butterflies dancing and heard the birds singing.

105
00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:44.732
One day his wings felt very strong.

106
00:05:45.472 --> 00:05:49.115
So he flapped them against his sides and flew high into the sky.

107
00:05:49.135 --> 00:05:54.740
"Wow, I can fly so high!

108
00:05:55.248 --> 00:05:56.568
What's happened to me?"

109
00:05:57.409 --> 00:06:00.150
The ugly duckling saw a beautiful garden with a pond.

110
00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:02.750
He decided to rest there for a while.

111
00:06:06.491 --> 00:06:10.213
Just then three swans swam out of the bushes by the pond.

112
00:06:10.993 --> 00:06:12.713
He remembered the beautiful birds.

113
00:06:14.214 --> 00:06:16.775
"I want to stay with these beautiful birds.

114
00:06:17.395 --> 00:06:20.956
But they will kill me because I am so ugly.

115
00:06:21.724 --> 00:06:25.646
At least I will die happily if I can be with them for a while."

116
00:06:27.187 --> 00:06:28.828
So he swam towards the swans.

117
00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:32.230
When the swans saw the young bird, they swam to him.

118
00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:36.272
"Peck me if you must!"

119
00:06:37.193 --> 00:06:39.734
And he bent his head down to the surface of the water.

120
00:06:40.575 --> 00:06:44.497
But the ugly duckling saw a beautiful swan looking back at him in the water!

121
00:06:44.517 --> 00:06:49.000
"Oh! Is that really me?

122
00:06:49.676 --> 00:06:51.857
I am a beautiful swan!

123
00:06:52.557 --> 00:06:55.239
I am not an ugly duckling after all!"

124
00:06:55.879 --> 00:06:58.120
The three swans welcomed the young swan.

125
00:07:01.181 --> 00:07:04.963
Some children came to the pond and threw pieces of bread into the water.

126
00:07:04.983 --> 00:07:09.385
"Look, there is another swan!

127
00:07:10.145 --> 00:07:13.186
This new one is the most beautiful of all."

128
00:07:15.267 --> 00:07:16.988
The ugly duckling was so happy.

129
00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:20.482
He was more beautiful than he had ever hoped to be.

130
00:07:21.323 --> 00:07:23.585
And now he knew where he belonged.
